  "title": "How to Pass Creación Digital I — UEM 2026-27",
  "slides": [
    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital I</h1><h2>Universidad Europea · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h · 80 h contact</em></p><p>Final event theme: <strong>Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?</strong></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official weights (guía)</h2><table><tr><th>Knowledge tests</th><td><strong>55%</strong></td></tr><tr><th>Case / problem</th><td><strong>15%</strong></td></tr><tr><th>Research &amp; projects</th><td><strong>20%</strong></td></tr><tr><th>Lab notebook</th><td><strong>10%</strong></td></tr></table><p>Studio deliverables map onto these instruments — they do not rewrite them.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Spanish cohort (coordination)</h2><p>Sandra Jiménez Duarte’s Plan de trabajo runs four continuous activities at <strong>11.2%</strong> each (Figurín · Key visual · <strong>Transposición cartel</strong> · revista). Compatible with our Labs/D map — does not replace the guía table.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Every session (order binding)</h2><ol><li><strong>Analysis strip</strong> — sessions 1–2: professor models analysis; from session 3: <strong>2 students × 15 min</strong> defence</li><li><strong>Masterclass</strong> — ideas + images</li><li><strong>Lab (Portfolio)</strong> — exercises + debates → portfolio</li><li><strong>Workshop (from session 4)</strong> — ≈ half D2 Transposition · ≈ half D3 final event</li></ol><p>Sessions 1–3: <em>no Workshop</em> — end after Lab. <em>Lab ≠ Workshop.</em></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Slide rule</h2><p>Before Lab exercises, a <strong>geometrical</strong> slide announces: exercises are coming and they go into your <strong>portfolio index</strong>.</p><p>Workshop open + outro also use geometrical backgrounds. Masterclass content uses accepted course media packs.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Five deliverables</h2><ol><li><strong>D1 Analysis</strong> — 15 min defence · slideshow · fashion image related to a <strong>Madrid exhibition</strong> piece</li><li><strong>D2 Transposition</strong> — <strong>same as ACT3:</strong> cartel from another language (song, film, poem, literary work, theatre…) · image series OK · source + process trail</li><li><strong>D3 Atrium</strong> — tech script + live defence · <em>What is fashion for you?</em></li><li><strong>D4 Portfolio index</strong> — Lab exercises + D1–D3</li><li><strong>D5 Exam</strong> — critical demonstration + portfolio self-review</li></ol>"},
    {"content":"<h2>D1 intra-rubric</h2><table><tr><th>Presentation</th><td>70%</td></tr><tr><th>Deliverable support</th><td>20%</td></tr><tr><th>Peer debate</th><td>10%</td></tr></table><p>Two students per session from session 3. Source files + process trail required.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Ordinary / extraordinary</h2><p>Binding dates: official UEM guide + Campus Virtual. Teaching evidence is not research data — exhibition needs consent.</p>","calendar_note":true},
    {"content":"<h2>Next step</h2><p>Start the portfolio index now. Prepare D1 around the Madrid visit brief. One transposition brief for both cohorts — ask before publishing student work.</p>"}
